---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Long Short Funds | Category III AIF | The Sovereign Ledger" currentPage="knowledge/aif">

<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pb-24">

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <nav class="py-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-outline border-b border-outline-variant/20 flex-wrap">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif" class="hover:text-secondary transition-colors">AIF Knowledge</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-outline-variant">chevron_right</span>
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-iii" class="hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Category III AIF</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-outline-variant">chevron_right</span>
    <span class="text-on-surface-variant">Long Short Funds</span>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 border-b border-outline-variant/20 mb-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-end">
      <div class="md:col-span-8">
        <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-secondary font-bold mb-3 block">Category III AIF · SEBI AIF Regulations, 2012</span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4 flex-wrap">
          <span class="text-[10px] px-3 py-1.5 bg-primary-container text-tertiary-fixed uppercase font-bold tracking-widest">Category III</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] px-3 py-1.5 bg-surface-container text-secondary border border-outline-variant/30 uppercase font-bold tracking-widest">Long / Short</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-headline text-primary-container leading-tight mb-6">
          Long Short <span class="italic font-light">Funds</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Long Short Category III AIFs simultaneously hold long positions in fundamentally undervalued stocks and short positions in overvalued ones — aiming to generate alpha from both directions of price movement while maintaining a managed net market exposure.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <div class="bg-primary-container p-8">
          <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-tertiary-fixed/70 block mb-4">Key Criteria</span>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            {[
              'Long undervalued + short overvalued stocks',
              'Net long exposure: typically 30–70%',
              'Shorts executed via F&O derivatives',
              'Absolute return orientation',
              'Fund-level taxation at MMR ~42.744%',
            ].map(item => (
              <li class="text-sm text-surface font-medium flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[14px] mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-tertiary-fixed">check_circle</span>{item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="mb-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
    <div class="md:col-span-5 bg-surface-container-low p-10">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-primary-container mb-6">How Long Short Works</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-loose mb-4">
        The Long Short strategy generates returns from two sources: the upward price movement of long positions (undervalued stocks expected to appreciate) and the downward price movement of short positions (overvalued stocks expected to decline). The difference in returns between longs and shorts — the "spread" — is the fund's alpha.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-loose">
        In India, short positions are typically implemented via single-stock futures or options from the F&O segment of NSE/BSE, rather than through actual stock borrowing (which is limited in India's Securities Lending and Borrowing mechanism). This has important implications for basis risk and roll costs.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 pt-8 border-t border-outline-variant/30">
        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-outline">Governing Regulation</span>
        <p class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container mt-1">SEBI AIF Regs, 2012 – Reg 3(4)(c)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-7">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-primary-container mb-6">Exposure Definitions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          { term: 'Gross Exposure', def: 'Total long positions + total short positions (notional). Typically 150–200% of NAV for active L/S funds. Measures how much total market risk the fund is taking.' },
          { term: 'Net Exposure', def: 'Long positions minus short positions, expressed as % of NAV. A net exposure of 50% means the fund behaves like a 50% invested long-only fund in a market move.' },
          { term: 'Gross Long', def: 'Sum of all long stock positions. The portion of the portfolio directly benefiting from a market rally.' },
          { term: 'Gross Short', def: 'Sum of all short positions (via F&O). The portion of the portfolio that profits from market or individual stock declines.' },
          { term: 'Alpha', def: 'The fund\'s return above what the net exposure to the market would explain. The skill-based return from stock selection on both long and short books.' },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="border-l-2 border-tertiary-fixed pl-4">
            <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-secondary block mb-1">{item.term}</span>
            <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">{item.def}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Approach -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-2">Portfolio Construction</h2>
    <div class="w-12 h-1 bg-primary-container mb-10"></div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      {[
        { icon: 'trending_up', title: 'Long Book', desc: 'High-conviction positions in fundamentally strong, undervalued businesses with near-term earnings catalysts. Typically 20–40 positions sized 2–7% each. Long tenure (12–24 months).' },
        { icon: 'trending_down', title: 'Short Book', desc: 'Positions in structurally challenged, overvalued, or deteriorating businesses. Implemented via NSE/BSE F&O. Held for shorter periods (1–6 months) with disciplined stop-losses.' },
        { icon: 'balance', title: 'Net Exposure Management', desc: 'The manager dynamically adjusts the ratio of longs to shorts based on market valuation, macro outlook, and risk appetite. More cautious markets → lower net exposure.' },
        { icon: 'shield', title: 'Tail Risk Hedging', desc: 'Index puts or VIX calls used to hedge extreme market events. These tail hedges reduce drawdowns during market crashes at the cost of carrying premiums in stable markets.' },
        { icon: 'analytics', title: 'Pair Trades', desc: 'Simultaneous long/short positions within the same sector (e.g., long HDFC Bank, short smaller private bank). Sector exposure is neutralised; returns driven purely by relative performance.' },
        { icon: 'event', title: 'Event-Driven Positions', desc: 'Catalytic events — results surprises, management changes, regulatory decisions, mergers — drive concentrated positions with defined timelines and exit triggers.' },
      ].map(step => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 border border-outline-variant/10">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary-container text-3xl mb-4 block">{step.icon}</span>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-primary-container mb-3">{step.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{step.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Characteristics -->
  <section class="mb-16 bg-primary-container text-surface px-8 md:px-12 py-12 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-64 h-64 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-3xl translate-x-1/3 -translate-y-1/3 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-10 relative z-10">Key <span class="italic">Characteristics at a Glance</span></h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 relative z-10">
      {[
        { label: 'Minimum Corpus',       value: '₹20 Crore',        sub: 'per scheme' },
        { label: 'Min. Investor Ticket', value: '₹1 Crore',         sub: '₹25L for employees' },
        { label: 'Net Exposure',         value: '30–70%',            sub: 'typical range' },
        { label: 'Gross Exposure',       value: '150–200%',          sub: 'of NAV, via F&O' },
        { label: 'Leverage',             value: 'Up to 2× NAV',      sub: 'SEBI circular 2021' },
        { label: 'Taxation',             value: 'Fund Level',        sub: 'MMR ~42.744%' },
        { label: 'Skin-in-the-Game',     value: '5% / ₹10 Cr',      sub: 'whichever is lower' },
        { label: 'Target Return',        value: '12–18% p.a.',       sub: 'absolute, net of fees' },
      ].map(p => (
        <div class="border border-secondary/30 p-5">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase font-label tracking-wider text-slate-400 mb-1">{p.label}</p>
          <p class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed leading-tight">{p.value}</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mt-1">{p.sub}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Risk Factors -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-6">Risk Considerations</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      {[
        { icon: 'swap_vert', title: 'Short Squeeze Risk', desc: 'Short positions can suffer unlimited theoretical losses if stock prices rise sharply. Short squeezes — driven by surprise earnings beats, corporate actions, or retail buying — are a significant risk.' },
        { icon: 'currency_rupee', title: 'F&O Basis & Roll Costs', desc: 'Indian shorts use futures/options rather than stock borrowing. Rolling short positions monthly incurs basis costs (futures premium), which can erode short-side profitability.' },
        { icon: 'percent', title: 'Fund-Level Tax Drag', desc: 'All income — including short-term gains from both long and short books — is taxed at MMR (~42.744%) at the fund level. This is the primary structural disadvantage vs PMS.' },
        { icon: 'bar_chart', title: 'Correlation in Stress', desc: 'In severe market sell-offs, all stocks tend to fall together. Shorts may not generate sufficient offsetting profits if correlations spike to 1.0. Net exposure management is critical.' },
      ].map(r => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 border border-outline-variant/10 flex gap-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary-container text-2xl shrink-0 mt-0.5">{r.icon}</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-container mb-2">{r.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{r.desc}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-primary-container text-white px-10 md:px-16 py-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-8 relative overflow-hidden mb-12">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-64 h-64 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-3xl translate-x-1/3 -translate-y-1/3 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="max-w-lg relative z-10">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-amber-100 mb-2">Explore Long Short Fund Opportunities</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Access SEBI-registered Category III Long Short AIFs through AlternaVest Capital's institutional platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 relative z-10">
      <a href="/explore" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-tertiary-fixed text-on-tertiary-fixed px-8 py-4 text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity">
        Browse Funds <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm">arrow_forward</span>
      </a>
      <button type="button" class="js-open-consult inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-white/30 text-white px-8 py-4 text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
        Speak to Advisor
      </button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Prev / Next -->
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-iii/long-only" class="flex-1 border border-outline p-5 hover:border-secondary transition-colors group text-center">
      <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-outline block mb-1">Previous</span>
      <span class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container group-hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Long Only Funds</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-iii/multi-strategy" class="flex-1 border border-outline p-5 hover:border-secondary transition-colors group text-center">
      <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-outline block mb-1">Next</span>
      <span class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container group-hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Multi-Strategy Funds</span>
    </a>
  </div>

</div>
</BaseLayout>
